    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the mineral trona, which is abundant in the dry lakebed of Searles Lake that borders Trona.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trona%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During World War I, Trona became the only reliable American source of potash, a key ingredient in gunpowder production.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trona%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Trona Pinnacles, a striking field of tufa spires, were designated a National Natural Landmark in 1968 and cost nothing to visit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
